data.content:
You were rickrolled because **`dQw4w9WgXcQ`** is the standard YouTube video ID for Rick Astley's *"Never Gonna Give You Up"*, and it was set as the default example video ID in the codebase:

### Where it comes from:
1. **Swagger / OpenAPI DTO Examples** (`src/meal-plan/dto/meal-plan-request.dto.ts`):
   ```typescript
   @ApiProperty({
     description: 'YouTube video id or full watch/shorts/embed URL',
     example: 'dQw4w9WgXcQ',
   })
   idOrUrl!: string;

   @ApiPropertyOptional({ example: 'Low-Sodium Veggie Stir Fry' })
   title?: string;
   ```
2. **README Curl Example** (`README.md`):
   The demo curl command uses `https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dQw4w9WgXcQ` paired with the title `"Low-Sodium Veggie Stir Fry"`.

### What happened:
- When using **Swagger UI** (`/api/docs`) with "Try it out" or running the example `curl` request without replacing `videoCandidates`, the API processed `dQw4w9WgXcQ`.
- The mock analyzer treated it as a safe `"Low-Sodium Veggie Stir Fry"` based on the sample title.
- The service returned the recommendation with the watch URL `https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dQw4w9WgXcQ`.
- Clicking the recommendation link opened YouTube directly to Rick Astley.

